      "provenance": "Pleiades",
      "associationCertaintyURI": "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/association-certainty/certain",
      "start": 1500,
      "details": "<p class=\"p1\"><em>Cez\u012bret\u00fc\u2019l-\u2018Arab</em>:\u00a0The boundaries of this province extend on the western side from the <em>Ba\u1e25r-i \u1e32ulz\u00fcm</em>\u00a0(<span>Red Sea</span>), along the regions of Yemen and the coast of the <em>\u1e24ij\u0101z</em>, up to <em>Eyle</em>.\u00a0From there, it reaches the regions of <em>\u015e\u0101m</em>\u00a0(Syria), and on the northern side, it includes part of the Syrian territories up to <em>B\u0101l\u012bs</em>, near\u00a0<em>\u1e24aleb</em> (Aleppo), and across the <em>Fur\u0101t</em> (Euphrates) to <em>Ra\u1e25be</em> and <em>\u02bf\u0100ne</em>.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"0\" data-end=\"1087\">...\u00a0In summary,\u00a0<em>Cez\u012bre-i \u2018Arab</em>\u00a0consists of five parts:\u00a0<em>Tih\u0101me, Necd,\u00a0</em>\u1e24ic\u0101z<em>, \u02bfAr\u016b\u1e0d</em>, and <em>Yemen</em>. (partially translated by the first creator of the name resource.)</p>",
